{"path":"string/byte/memcmp","title":"memcmp","titleHtml":"memcmp","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/string/byte/memcmp","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"Compares the first count bytes of the objects pointed to by lhs and rhs. The comparison is done lexicographically.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte\"><code>&lt;string.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> memcmp<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> lhs, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> rhs, <a href=\"/w/c/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw100\">size_t</span></a> count <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Compares the first <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">count</span></code> bytes of the objects pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">lhs</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">rhs</span></code>. The comparison is done lexicographically.\n</p><p>The sign of the result is the sign of the difference between the values of the first pair of bytes (both interpreted as <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span>) that differ in the objects being compared.\n</p><p>The behavior is undefined if access occurs beyond the end of either object pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">lhs</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">rhs</span></code>. The behavior is undefined if either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">lhs</span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">rhs</span></code> is a null pointer.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> lhs, rhs\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointers to the objects to compare\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> count\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> number of bytes to examine\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Negative value if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">lhs</span></code>  appears before <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">rhs</span></code> in lexicographical order.\n</p><p>Zero if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">lhs</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">rhs</span></code> compare equal, or if count is zero.\n</p><p>Positive value if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">lhs</span></code> appears after <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">rhs</span></code> in lexicographical order.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This function reads <a href=\"/w/c/language/object\">object representations</a>, not the object values, and is typically meaningful for byte arrays only: structs may have padding bytes whose values are indeterminate, the values of any bytes beyond the last stored member in a union are indeterminate, and a type may have two or more representations for the same value (different encodings for <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"sy2\">+</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span></span></code> or for <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"sy2\">+</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">–<span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span></span></code>, indeterminate padding bits within the type).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> demo<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> lhs, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> rhs, <a href=\"/w/c/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw100\">size_t</span></a> sz<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw100\">size_t</span></a> n <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> sz<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/c/io/putchar\"><span class=\"kw834\">putchar</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>lhs<span class=\"br0\">[</span>n<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> rc <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> memcmp<span class=\"br0\">(</span>lhs, rhs, sz<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>rel <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> rc <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span> <span class=\"sy4\">?</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" precedes \"</span> <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> rc <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span> <span class=\"sy4\">?</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" follows \"</span> <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" compares equal \"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fputs\"><span class=\"kw831\">fputs</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>rel, <a href=\"/w/c/io/std_streams\"><span class=\"kw886\">stdout</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw100\">size_t</span></a> n <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> sz<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/c/io/putchar\"><span class=\"kw834\">putchar</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>rhs<span class=\"br0\">[</span>n<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/puts\"><span class=\"kw835\">puts</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\" in lexicographical order\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> a1<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">'a'</span>,<span class=\"st0\">'b'</span>,<span class=\"st0\">'c'</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> a2<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span> a1<span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">'a'</span>,<span class=\"st0\">'b'</span>,<span class=\"st0\">'d'</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    demo<span class=\"br0\">(</span>a1, a2, <span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span> a1<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    demo<span class=\"br0\">(</span>a2, a1, <span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span> a1<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    demo<span class=\"br0\">(</span>a1, a1, <span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span> a1<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>abc precedes abd in lexicographical order\nabd follows abc in lexicographical order\nabc compares equal to abc in lexicographical order</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-23\">\n<ul><li> C23 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.24.4.1 The memcmp function (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.24.4.1 The memcmp function (p: 266)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.24.4.1 The memcmp function (p: 365)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.21.4.1 The memcmp function (p: 328)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c89\">\n<ul><li> C89/C90 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1990): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 4.11.4.1 The memcmp function \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strcmp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strcmp</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   compares two strings <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strncmp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strncmp</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   compares a certain amount of characters of two strings <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/memcmp\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>memcmp</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"string","title":"Strings library"},{"path":"string/byte","title":"Null-terminated byte strings"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"memcmp","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Compares the first count bytes of the objects pointed to by lhs and rhs."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"lhs, rhs, count"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Negative value if lhs appears before rhs in lexicographical order."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This function reads object representations, not the object values, and is typically meaningful for byte arrays only: structs may have padding bytes whose…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"strcmp","note":"compares two strings"},{"label":"strncmp","note":"compares a certain amount of characters of two strings"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":408,"codeBlockCount":2}
